Compare naive/semi-naive evaluation and native/desugared morphisms
after repeated edits and closures. Fix supplied inputs during
isomorphism search so renaming cannot hide different consequences.

Use direct Rust tests for merged witnesses, morphism diamonds, and
nested images. Generate typed theories and seeded operation sequences;
save failing theories and traces for replay. Vary morphism endpoints,
partial image maps, late facts, and equalities.
Include both reflexive equalities and equalities between distinct
variables.

Dispatch runtime-typed edits to setters on persistent compiled models.
Reimporting facts between closures would reset incremental state and
could mask evaluation bugs.
